Third-party fonts
=================

The firmware embeds bitmap subsets of fonts released under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1. The subsets are
generated by tools/fonts.sh (lv_font_conv, 4 bpp) from google/fonts at commit 45e3d5269e4a17d823f6d84470bc084dc5ae46f6
and committed as C sources:

    firmware/components/watch_ui/fonts/font_*.c
    firmware/apps/omni/main/ui/fonts/font_*.c

Text in some of the exported art (firmware/apps/*/assets, tools/export) is also set in these fonts.

- IBM Plex Sans and IBM Plex Mono (font_plex_sans_*, font_plex_mono_*)
  Copyright (c) 2017 IBM Corp. with Reserved Font Name "Plex".
  Licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1: LICENSES/OFL-IBMPlex.txt.

- Cormorant SC (font_cormorant_*)
  Copyright 2015 the Cormorant Project Authors (github.com/CatharsisFonts/Cormorant).
  Licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1: LICENSES/OFL-CormorantSC.txt.

- UnifrakturMaguntia (the motto in the Omni's lid art only; tools/export/fonts)
  Copyright (c) 2010, j. 'mach' wust, with Reserved Font Name UnifrakturMaguntia. Copyright (c) 2009, Peter Wiegel.
  Licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1: tools/export/fonts/OFL.txt.

- Saira Stencil One, VT323 and Chakra Petch (the Mining Ship theme's art only: drawn into the glyph atlases and images
  in firmware/apps/rd/assets by tools/rd_export.mjs; tools/fonts.sh fetches the TTFs and checks their licences)
  Saira Stencil One: Copyright 2019 The Saira Stencil Project Authors
  (https://github.com/Omnibus-Type/Saira/SairaStencil).
  VT323: Copyright 2011, The VT323 Project Authors (peter.hull@oikoi.com).
  Chakra Petch: Copyright 2018 The Chakra Petch Project Authors (https://github.com/m4rc1e/Chakra-Petch.git).
  Licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1: tools/font_licences/SairaStencilOne-OFL.txt,
  tools/font_licences/VT323-OFL.txt and tools/font_licences/ChakraPetch-OFL.txt.

The license files above are the upstream ones, verbatim (the IBM Plex one with its line endings made LF). The subsets'
symbol names are internal identifiers; no font is offered to users under a Reserved Font Name.

Imagery
=======

The Omni's globe textures (design/assets/earth-{day,night}-1024.jpg, the copies in design/mockups/assets, and
firmware/apps/omni/assets/earth512.tex and omni512.tex made from them by tools/gen_tex.mjs) are downscaled from NASA
imagery, which is in the public domain:

- Day: NASA Visible Earth, The Blue Marble (2002), land surface, ocean color and sea ice (land_ocean_ice_2048.jpg).
  NASA Goddard Space Flight Center; image by Reto Stoeckli, enhancements by Robert Simmon.
  https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/the-blue-marble-true-color-global-imagery-at-1km-resolution/
  https://assets.science.nasa.gov/content/dam/science/esd/eo/content-feature/bluemarble/images/land_ocean_ice_2048.jpg

- Night: NASA Earth at Night 2012 (Black Marble), dnb_land_ocean_ice.2012.13500x6750.jpg.
  NASA Earth Observatory / NASA Goddard Space Flight Center, Suomi NPP VIIRS.
  https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/earth-at-night/maps/
  https://assets.science.nasa.gov/content/dam/science/esd/eo/images/imagerecords/79000/79765/dnb_land_ocean_ice.2012.13500x6750.jpg

Public domain; NASA Earth Observatory / NASA Goddard Space Flight Center. NASA does not endorse this project.

Code
====

The AXP2101 power-manager driver (firmware/components/board/axp2101.c and axp2101.h) is a C port of the register reads
and interrupt handling in Waveshare's example for this board, examples/esp-idf/01_AXP2101 (port_axp2101.cpp and
axp2101_registers.h) in https://github.com/waveshareteam/ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-1.75C.
  Copyright 2026 Waveshare.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0: LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.
  Changes: ported from C++ to C on ESP-IDF's i2c_master driver; only the battery gauge, charge state, VBUS and
  power-key interrupt parts are kept (the example's rail and charger configuration is not ported).

Components fetched at build time
================================

These are not in this repository. The IDF Component Manager downloads them on the first build, at the versions pinned
in firmware/apps/*/dependencies.lock, into firmware/apps/*/managed_components, and each keeps its own licence file
there. The firmware images built from this repository contain code from them.

- ESP-IDF v5.5.6 (the SDK, its components and the Unity test framework the host tests use), Espressif Systems:
  Apache License 2.0 (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt); some of its components carry their own licences, listed in ESP-IDF.
- LVGL 9.5.0 (lvgl/lvgl): MIT licence, Copyright (c) 2025 LVGL Kft: LICENSES/MIT-LVGL.txt.
- The Waveshare board support package waveshare/esp32_s3_touch_amoled_1_75c 3.0.0, and waveshare/esp_lcd_touch_cst9217
  2.0.0 and waveshare/qmi8658 2.0.2: Apache License 2.0.
- Espressif components, Apache License 2.0: espressif/esp_mmap_assets 2.0.1 (the assets partition image and its
  build-time packer), button 4.2.2, cmake_utilities 0.5.3, esp_codec_dev 1.5.11, esp_io_expander 1.2.1, esp_lcd_co5300
  2.2.0, esp_lcd_panel_io_additions 1.0.1~1, esp_lcd_touch 1.2.1, esp_lv_decoder 0.4.3, esp_lv_fs 1.0.1,
